in its conclusions the council sets out  a series of initiatives to reduce waste  and losses in the future these measures  include the improvement of monitoring  and data collection to better understand  the problem enhancing the use of biomass  in future EU legislation and to  facilitate the donation of unsold food  products to charities we adopted Council  conclusions on two evaluations by the  Commission and had an exchange of views  on the future of EU forest policy the  debate in the council confirms that the  issues related to forests are highly  relevant and that extra EU actions need  to be taken and need to be further  discussed these Council conclusions mark  an important step forward in the fight  against deforestation and illegal timber  on the Commissioner Olivia already  implementing an action plan to support  effort efforts to reduce food waste in  the near future will propose a  harmonized methodology to measure food  waste this will be crucial to actually  monitor our efforts and defiant  effective food food based prevention  strategies in the autumn I will launch a  platform on food waste which will gather  all interested parties with the aim of  sharing with practices and evaluation of  progress made over time within a system  of integrated pest management we want to  favor prevention non-chemical methods  biological controls and low-risk  products whenever as this is possible so  it is important that all stakeholders  make an effort to increase the  availability of sustainable alternatives  the Commission had made an ambitious  proposal answer conditions of use of  glyphosate in particular they have  recommended that follow them to the  Member States a band of a conformal and  called tallava mean from glyphosate  based products to minimize the use in  public parks public play grounds and  gardens and to minimize a pre-harvest  use of glyphosate let me stress my huge  surprise to see that member state could  not adopt these measures of Health  Protection yesterday
 

